  "body": "## What's new in v0.2.0\n\n### Full Apple Vision surface\n\nFive new subcommands that wrap Apple's built-in Vision framework — no model downloads, all on-device:\n\n- `face-landmarks <image>` — 13 landmark region groups per face (eyes, eyebrows, nose, lips, pupils, contour)\n- `pose <image>` — 18-joint body pose skeleton (nose, neck, shoulders, elbows, wrists, hips, knees, ankles)\n- `humans <image>` — full-body rectangle detection\n- `annotate <image> \"keyword\"` — OCR keyword find + draw red boxes; `--precision character` enables per-character bbox (dual Vision request + Y-clustering)\n- `infer <model> <image>` — CoreML model runner, downloads from GitHub Release on first use\n\n### `salient` — major upgrades\n\nFour overlay styles (was 1):\n- `--overlay` (default): 5-band topographic contours (red→yellow→green→cyan→blue)\n- `--overlay-red`: red heatmap on faded original (eye-grabbing)\n- `--overlay-jet`: full 5-segment Jet colormap (academic standard)\n- `--overlay-bw`: B&W background + colormap (paper-style)\n\nSmart crop to social-media presets:\n- `--crop` — find saliency bbox, output cropped image\n- `--size square|story|reel|wide|linkedin-cover|twitter-header|yt-thumb|ig-landscape|ig-portrait|avatar|avatar-2x|pinterest`\n- Or custom WxH like `--size 1080x1080`\n\nOCR text inside saliency:\n- `--ocr` returns only texts overlapping the salient region\n- Useful for \"extract the text from the part of the image the user is looking at\"\n\n### `ocr` — TSV default, multiple output flavors\n\n- Default is TSV: `text\\tconfidence\\tbbox\\tnorm\\tcenter\\tcenter_norm` — pipes cleanly into spreadsheets/tools\n- `--text` — one text per line\n- `--lines` — grouped by visual lines (configurable tolerance via `--tolerance`)\n- `--json` — full JSON with all info\n\n### `ocr` — agent-facing workflow\n\n```sh\n# Read text from a screenshot — straight into an LLM\nmacvision ocr shot.png --tsv\n\n# Get the words (no boxes)\nmacvision ocr shot.png --text | head\n\n# Group by visual lines\nmacvision ocr shot.png --lines\n```\n\n### `classify` — animal-species specialization\n\n- `--animals` uses `VNRecognizeAnimalsRequest` (Apple's animal detector): cat/dog/bird/etc.\n\n### README + tldr — agent-focused\n\nEach subcommand's `--help` has a `tldr:` block with agent-style examples. Root `macvision --help` lists top-level agent workflows:\n\n```sh\nmacvision classify photo.jpg --top 5        # what's in this photo?\nmacvision ocr shot.png --tsv                # read a screenshot for an LLM\nmacvision detect shot.png --ocr --lang ...  # full screenshot dump\nmacvision face-landmarks portrait.jpg       # detect face features\nmacvision pose runner.jpg                   # body pose skeleton\nmacvision annotate doc.png X-CMD --output marked.png  # mark all \"X-CMD\" mentions\nmacvision salient photo.jpg --crop --size story     # smart-thumb for social\nmacvision doctor                            # check Vision capabilities\n```\n\n19 tests pass; CI green (build-and-test, license/cla).\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/ljh-sh/macvision/compare/v0.1.4...v0.2.0\n"
